id: pm-javbsq
title: "GH-1178: history hashes exclude record author and agent provenance, so attribution can be rewritten without detection"
description: "GitHub issue #1178 reproduces on pm-cli 2026.9.2: editing a history record's ts, author, author_source, op, or agent_provenance does not alter the item patch hashes. After uncached verification, pm health --strict-exit and pm history --verify --strict-exit still report clean. The ledger therefore proves item-state replay but not the immutable attribution and operation metadata that describes who performed it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: "area:history","area:sdk",context-integrity,github-1178,immutability,provenance,security
created_at: "2026-09-02T21:14:35.285Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-03T06:08:28.310Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-03T05:56:55.531Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-03T05:56:55.531Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "Define a versioned canonical hash envelope covering at least timestamp, author, author_source, operation, and agent provenance; preserve explicit backward verification for legacy histories without claiming they cover attribution; supply a documented, audited migration and repair boundary; add a negative control that changes only author or provenance and must fail history verification and health; compose with re-anchoring preservation instead of erasing original evidence; pass history, merge, restore, SDK, CLI, security, static, and exact coverage gates."
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: critical
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1178
severity: critical
environment: pm-cli 2026.9.2 with a fresh single-entry item history stream
repro_steps: "Create an item, edit only the stored history record author and agent_provenance fields, remove the drift cache, then run pm health --strict-exit and pm history <id> --verify --strict-exit; both exit zero."
resolution: "Sealed immutable history envelopes over attribution, operation, context, patch, and item anchors; verified them in replay and every rewrite path; retained reconstructable prior-record evidence with privacy-safe digest-only degradation during sensitive redaction."
expected_result: Author or provenance-only tampering fails verification while legacy item-state-only streams remain truthfully compatible.
actual_result: "Author-only tampering is rejected by CLI health/history and SDK verification; legacy coverage is explicit; 8,318 tests pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and packed SDK consumers pass."
component: "Core history ledger, SDK verification, health, and repair compatibility"
customer_impact: "Reviewers and agents can receive a green integrity verdict after attribution was modified during merge, rebase, or manual repair."
