comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-02T21:14:35.285Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status searches for author/provenance hash coverage, attribution tampering, history epochs, and immutable record fields found open pm-aka8m7 for retaining original anchors during re-anchoring and open pm-9yfo for mutation-history completeness. Neither covers the record envelope itself. GitHub #1178 is the canonical owner for the demonstrated green-verifier attribution rewrite. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1178"
  "2026-09-02T21:14:59.271Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence: issue #1178 now points to this canonical item at the merge-stable main-branch toon path."
  "2026-09-03T05:35:06.469Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: every newly written history record is sealed with a versioned canonical record hash covering attribution, operation, context, patch, and item anchors. Replay, health, redaction, repair, compaction, and provenance normalization verify the immutable envelope before rewriting; rewrite evidence reconstructs retained prior envelopes and rejects author, patch, or record tampering. Full gate: 600 files, 8,318 tests, 100/100/100/100 coverage."
  "2026-09-03T05:46:55.822Z","harness:codex","Manual temporary-directory acceptance passed: the packed package launched through both npx and bunx, installed 13 bundled packages, and compiled a strict external TypeScript consumer; the 88-command package-first dogfood passed; a dedicated isolated probe verified public SDK record hashing, author-only tamper refusal, stale exact-pin reads, stale exact-pin mutation refusal with project_runtime_history_epoch_incompatible, PM_ALLOW_STALE_CLI override, child-cwd Claude session discovery without path leakage, and legacy receipt acceptance."
  "2026-09-03T06:08:28.310Z","harness:codex","Governance evidence: the final real-tracker static run correctly failed closed until whole-record integrity closure was bound to executable prevention evidence. Author, time, operation, context, patch, and anchor tampering are negative controls across replay/rewrite tests, exact coverage, record-integrity assurance, and hosted static/coverage checks; no waiver is used."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T05:35:07.060Z","harness:codex","Compatibility note: legacy records remain explicitly item-state-only evidence. The new verifier does not overclaim attribution integrity for an epoch that never stored a record envelope."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-03T05:35:07.551Z","harness:codex","Item-state hashes prove replay results, not who performed an operation or what immutable metadata accompanied it. A record envelope must be separately versioned, and any maintenance rewrite must preserve enough prior-envelope material for independent verification."
